From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: restore Trek Tech wireframe movie dimensions

The exterior location has no 03WbegQ.mov.  Its missing opening wireframe can
leave puppet sprite 19 carrying stale stretched dimensions when the valid
08WendQ.mov destination movie is assigned, rendering that movie as vertical
strips.

Trek Tech uses sprite 19 exclusively for 180x155 wireframe movies.  Clear its
stale stretch state before assigning a digital-video cast, then restore the
native dimensions after setCast has loaded the movie and learned its actual
size.  This retains the sprite's authored stage position.  Other sprites,
games, videos, and custom puppet sizing are unchanged.
---
 engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp
--- a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp
@@ -1926,6 +1926,19 @@ void Lingo::setTheSprite(Datum &id1, int field, Datum &d) {
 			// Since Digital Video dimensions get clarified after loading,
 			// we enforce them here
 			if (castId != sprite->_castId || (castMember && castMember->_type == kCastDigitalVideo)) {
+				// Trek Tech always authors its wireframe movies at their native
+				// 180x155 size.  The exterior has no 03WbegQ.mov, so sprite 19 can
+				// otherwise carry stale stretched dimensions into 08WendQ.mov and
+				// render the destination wireframe as vertical strips.  The movie's
+				// true dimensions are not available until setCast loads it, so reset
+				// this dedicated sprite both before and after assignment.
+				bool resetTrekTechWireframeSize = id == 19 && castMember &&
+						castMember->_type == kCastDigitalVideo &&
+						Common::String(g_director->getGameId()).equals("trektech");
+				if (resetTrekTechWireframeSize)
+					sprite->_stretch = false;
 				channel->setCast(castId);
+				if (resetTrekTechWireframeSize)
+					channel->setStretch(false);
 			}
 		}
